{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Disabled","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this component to take an entity out of play for a while without despawning it, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an enemy waiting off screen. A disabled entity keeps its components and stays live, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reading it directly through its handle still works. A query or update reaches it only when it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads or writes "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Disabled"},{"type":"text","text":", names it in a filter, or allows it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryFilter\/allowing(_:)-swift.type.method"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","let enemy = world.spawn(Position(x: 5, y: 5))","","world.insert(Disabled(), into: enemy)","print(world.query(Position.self).count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\"","print(world.query(Position.self).allowing(Disabled.self).count)","\/\/ Prints \"2\"","","world.remove(Disabled.self, from: enemy)","print(world.query(Position.self).count)","\/\/ Prints \"2\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To make your own component types behave like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Disabled"},{"type":"text","text":", register them with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/registerDisablingComponent(_:)",